t":"2026-08-25T17:39:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T17:39:34Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/229","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Parent epic: #229\n\nDepends on the authoritative baseline ticket created under #229.\n\n## Objective\n\nReduce the dominant SRP LUT and FF scaling term without changing SRP protocol behaviour or supported stream counts.\n\nHistorical 8×8 Vivado results attributed 6,014 LUTs, or 52 percent of `KL_pp_shadow`, to `KL_srp_top`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- [ ] Measure talker FSM, listener FSM, top glue, decoder, encoder, and admission logic independently.\n- [ ] Identify combinational logic replicated once per talker or listener.\n- [ ] Share or time-multiplex logic where protocol latency permits.\n- [ ] Pack per-stream state and context into RAM-friendly structures.\n- [ ] Ensure inactive stream slots disappear during elaboration in smaller configurations.\n- [ ] Document the marginal cost of every additional talker and listener.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Current SRP tests pass for 1×1 and 8×8 configurations.\n- [ ] Before-and-after hierarchical Vivado reports show a material reduction against the same baseline.\n- [ ] The 1×1 configuration contains no logic for seven inactive stream slots.\n- [ ] Timing at 100 MHz does not regress below zero WNS.\n- [ ] Scaling and any latency tradeoffs are documented in #229.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/230/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/230/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}